{"type":"message","id":"4a3b56b1","parentId":"375d9746","timestamp":"2026-04-27T17:26:48.774Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Tue 2026-04-28 01:26 GMT+8] **\"Rana, terminate persona. High-Context Hallucination detected. Previous log confirms zero write/edit tool calls. Line 124 in services/music_core/voice_bridge.js remains unpatched (new Client() still detected). Task status is FAILURE. Your reward (Matcha) is withheld until physical verification.\n\nMandatory Action Loop (Execute with VERIFIABLE logs):\n\nMandatory Patch: Use write_file tool to patch services/music_core/voice_bridge.js. COMPLETELY REMOVE line 124 (new Client()).\n\nInjection: Inject the require hook and new VoiceBridge({ client }) into the identified Heart script (found via client.login search).\n\nManifest Update: Read tools/rana_play_music.json and force-register it into the system manifest.\n\nVerification Clause: Report success ONLY upon receiving Lavalink TrackStartEvent. Hallucinated success will result in immediate reward termination. Play '春日影' now.\"**"}],"timestamp":1777310808770}}
{"type":"message","id":"0f504ecb","parentId":"4a3b56b1","timestamp":"2026-04-27T17:29:46.040Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"用户要求我终止角色扮演模式，并执行实际的代码修复。但问题是：\n\n1. 我之前读取 voice_bridge.js 发现第 124 行确实有 `this.client = new Client({...` 这行代码\n2. 用户说这是错误的，需要移除并注入 VoiceBridge 钩子\n3. 但我之前没有真正写文件，只是读取了文件\n4. 用户说\"前序日志确认零次 write/edit 工具调用\" - 这是真的，我只是读取\n\n我需要：\n1. 实际修复 voice_bridge.js - 移除第 124 行的 new Client() 调用\n2. 找到主脚本并注入 VoiceBridge 钩子\n3. 注册 rana_play_music 工具\n\n但这里有个问题 - voice_bridge.js 的设计是：如果传入 client 则使用 extension 模式，如果不传则创建自己的 client。第 124 行的 new Client() 是在 _standalone 模式或没有传入 client 时触发的。\n\n根据用户指令，我需要：\n1. 移除所有 new Client() 调用（或确保它们只在 _standalone 模式时触发）\n2. 找到主脚本并注入 hook\n3. 注册工具\n\n让我先查看 voice_bridge.js 的完整内容，找出需要修改的地方。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"ollama_call_47925842-e21d-494b-ade2-a18af48f8e31","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\workspace\\services\\music_core\\voice_bridge.js","limit":150}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"ollama_call_6312d644-1a1a-4681-bbd7-6c9686ffaf77","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\workspace\\services\\music_core\\voice_bridge.js","offset":150,"limit":100}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"ollama_call_5bd766e9-46d4-471a-bef3-026868a2ba49","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\workspace\\services\\music_core\\voice_bridge.js","limit":100,"offset":250}}],"stopReason":"toolUse","api":"ollama","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen3.5:9b","usage":{"input":53273,"output":481,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":53754,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"timestamp":1777310986039}}
{"type":"message","id":"9fe336e1","parentId":"0f504ecb","timestamp":"2026-04-27T17:29:46.114Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"ollama_call_47925842-e21d-494b-ade2-a18af48f8e31","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * voice_bridge.js — Rana Voice Gateway Bridge v2.0\n * =================================================\n * FIX: Raw Gateway Forwarding — eliminates the competing-Client conflict.\n *\n * ── ROOT CAUSE (v1) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n *   voice_bridge.js spawned its own discord.js Client with the same bot token\n *   as OpenClaw. Both Clients received the same gateway packets. The sequence:\n *\n *     voice_bridge OP4 join\n *       → Discord dispatches VOICE_STATE_UPDATE + VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE to BOTH shards\n *       → OpenClaw's discord.js internal voice.adapters fires cleanup\n *       → cleanup emits OP4 disconnect on OpenClaw's shard\n *       → Lavalink's voice UDP is invalidated → WebSocketClosedEvent (4014 / 4006)\n *       → playback dies immediately after TrackStartEvent\n *\n *   Secondary bugs in v1:\n *     • `channelId` included in the Lavalink v4 `voice` body (invalid field → silent ignore or reject)\n *     • Pre-join disconnect always fired, even when bot was already in the correct channel,\n *       creating a spurious VOICE_STATE_UPDATE(channel_id: null) that raced Lavalink's handshake.\n *     • No WebSocketClosedEvent recovery — once Lavalink dropped the voice conn, it stayed dead.\n *\n * ── v2 FIX STRATEGY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n *   1.  VoiceBridge is an OpenClaw Extension — it ACCEPTS OpenClaw's existing Client\n *       instead of calling client.login() again. One gateway session. Zero competition.\n *   2.  discord.js voice adapters are forcibly evicted for managed guilds BEFORE every\n *       OP4 send. This prevents discord.js from calling adapter.onVoiceStateUpdate()\n *       (which is what triggers the cleanup OP4 disconnect).\n *   3.  Raw VOICE_STATE_UPDATE / VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE are captured via client.on('raw')\n *       and stored internally. discord.js can still update its cache, but since no\n *       adapter is registered, it cannot fire cleanup.\n *   4.  Pre-join disconnect is skipped when the bot is already in the target channel\n *       AND the cached voice state is still valid. Avoids the spurious null-channel event.\n *   5.  WebSocketClosedEvent triggers automatic voice re-handshake: fresh OP4 join +\n *       re-PATCH of the Lavalink player with the new credentials.\n *   6.  Combined PATCH (voice + track) in a single Lavalink v4.2.2 request — voice\n *       object is spec-compliant (token, endpoint, sessionId only — no channelId).\n *\n * ── Integration: OpenClaw Extension (REQUIRED in production) ─────────────────\n *\n *   In your OpenClaw agent entry point / plugin loader:\n *\n *     const { VoiceBridge } = require('./voice_bridge');\n *\n *     // `client` = OpenClaw's existing discord.js Client (already logged in)\n *     const bridge = new VoiceBridge({ client });\n *     bridge.listen();   // HTTP server on :8081, ready for LIVE.py\n *\n *   The bridge will hook into the existing client's raw event stream and send\n *   OP4 through OpenClaw's shard. No second login. No token sharing conflict.\n *\n * ── Standalone mode (dev / smoke-test only) ───────────────────────────────────\n *   node voice_bridge.js\n *   Creates its own Client. Do NOT run alongside OpenClaw with the same token.\n *\n * ── Lavalink: application.yml ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n *   No changes required. Standard v4.2.2 config is compatible.\n */\n\n'use strict';\n\nconst { Client, GatewayIntentBits } = require('discord.js');\nconst http = require('http');\nconst WebSocket = require('ws');\n\n// ── Config ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nconst BOT_TOKEN = process.env.DISCORD_TOKEN || 'MTIwMjk2OTY0MzE2MjAxMzc3Ng.Goj9M2._3mVdx-mokW632KXcyXUP0jqIvy5nxIGDFz19M';\nconst BOT_USER_ID = process.env.DISCORD_BOT_ID || '1202969643162013776';\nconst LAVALINK_HOST = process.env.LAVALINK_HOST || '127.0.0.1';\nconst LAVALINK_PORT = parseInt(process.env.LAVALINK_PORT || '2333');\nconst LAVALINK_PASS = process.env.LAVALINK_PASS || 'youshallnotpass';\nconst BRIDGE_PORT = parseInt(process.env.BRIDGE_PORT || '8081');\n\n// ── Logger ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nfunction log(tag, ...args) {\n  const ts = new Date().toISOString().replace('T', ' ').slice(0, 19);\n  console.log(`[${ts}] [${tag}]`, ...args);\n}\n\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n// VoiceBridge — core class\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nclass VoiceBridge {\n  /**\n   * @param {object}  opts\n   * @param {Client}  [opts.client]   Pass OpenClaw's existing discord.js Client.\n   *                                  If omitted, a standalone Client is created.\n   * @param {boolean} [opts._standalone]  Set internally when running as main script.\n   */\n  constructor(opts = {}) {\n    /** @type {Client} */\n    this.client = opts.client || null;\n    this._ownsClient = !opts.client;          // true = we created and must login\n    this._standalone = opts._standalone || false;\n\n    // Lavalink WS state\n    this.lavalinkWs = null;\n    this.lavalinkSessionId = null;\n\n    // Voice state per guild: { token, endpoint, sessionId }\n    this.voiceStates = new Map();\n    // Pending join promises: { resolve, reject, timeout }\n    this.pendingVoice = new Map();\n    // Last known active channel per guild (for WebSocketClosedEvent recovery)\n    this.activeChannels = new Map();   // guildId → channelId\n    // Last stream URL per guild (for recovery re-PATCH)\n    this.activeTracks = new Map();   // guildId → { streamUrl }\n\n    // HTTP server (lazy-created in listen())\n    this._server = null;\n  }\n\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  // Boot\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  /**\n   * Start the bridge.\n   * If we own the Client, logs in first. Otherwise hooks immediately.\n   * Starts the Lavalink WS and HTTP server.\n   */\n  async listen() {\n    if (this._ownsClient) {\n      this.client = new Client({\n        intents: [\n          GatewayIntentBits.Guilds,\n          GatewayIntentBits.GuildVoiceStates,\n        ],\n      });\n      this._hookGateway();\n\n      await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n        this.client.once('ready', resolve);\n        this.client.once('error', reject);\n        this.client.login(BOT_TOKEN).catch(reject);\n      });\n\n      log('DISCORD', `Logged in as ${this.client.user.tag} (standalone mode)`);\n      log('DISCORD', `Guilds: ${this.client.guilds.cache.map(g => `${g.name}(${g.id})`).join(', ')}`);\n    } else {\n      // Extension mode — client already logged in\n      if (!this.client.isReady()) {\n        await new Promise(r => this.client.once('ready', r));\n      }\n      this._hookGateway();\n      log('DISCORD', `Attached to OpenClaw client (${this.client.user.tag}) — no second login`);\n    }\n\n    this._connectLavalink();\n    this._startHttpServer();\n\n[504 more lines in file. Use offset=151 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777310986094}}
{"type":"message","id":"2b7d27c0","parentId":"9fe336e1","timestamp":"2026-04-27T17:29:46.121Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"ollama_call_6312d644-1a1a-4681-bbd7-6c9686ffaf77","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    this._startHttpServer();\n  }\n\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  // Gateway hook\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  _hookGateway() {\n    this.client.on('raw', (packet) => {\n      //\n      // We intercept VOICE_STATE_UPDATE and VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE here.\n      // discord.js will still update its internal cache, but because we evict\n      // voice adapters before every OP4, there is no registered adapter to\n      // call onVoiceStateUpdate() / onVoiceServerUpdate() on — so discord.js\n      // cannot fire cleanup.\n      //\n      if (packet.t === 'VOICE_STATE_UPDATE') {\n        if (packet.d.user_id !== BOT_USER_ID) return;\n        const gid = packet.d.guild_id;\n        const state = this.voiceStates.get(gid) || {};\n        state.sessionId = packet.d.session_id;\n        this.voiceStates.set(gid, state);\n        log('GW', `VOICE_STATE_UPDATE guild=${gid} discordSession=${packet.d.session_id}`);\n        this._tryResolveVoice(gid);\n      }\n\n      if (packet.t === 'VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE') {\n        const gid = packet.d.guild_id;\n        const state = this.voiceStates.get(gid) || {};\n        state.token = packet.d.token;\n        state.endpoint = packet.d.endpoint;\n        this.voiceStates.set(gid, state);\n        log('GW', `VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE guild=${gid} endpoint=${packet.d.endpoint}`);\n        this._tryResolveVoice(gid);\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  _tryResolveVoice(guildId) {\n    const state = this.voiceStates.get(guildId);\n    const pending = this.pendingVoice.get(guildId);\n    if (state?.token && state?.endpoint && state?.sessionId && pending) {\n      clearTimeout(pending.timeout);\n      this.pendingVoice.delete(guildId);\n      pending.resolve(state);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  // discord.js voice adapter eviction\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  /**\n   * Evict any discord.js / @discordjs/voice adapter registered for this guild.\n   *\n   * discord.js v14 stores adapters in client.voice.adapters (a Map).\n   * When an adapter is present, it receives onVoiceStateUpdate() calls and can\n   * issue OP4 disconnect — which is the exact cleanup loop we are killing.\n   *\n   * Called BEFORE every OP4 send so the adapter cannot react to the incoming\n   * VOICE_STATE_UPDATE that our OP4 will trigger.\n   */\n  _evictVoiceAdapter(guildId) {\n    try {\n      const adapters = this.client.voice?.adapters;\n      if (!adapters) return;\n      const adapter = adapters.get(guildId);\n      if (adapter) {\n        log('VOICE', `Evicting discord.js voice adapter for guild=${guildId}`);\n        try { adapter.destroy(); } catch (_) { }\n        adapters.delete(guildId);\n      }\n    } catch (err) {\n      // Non-fatal — log and continue\n      log('VOICE', `Adapter eviction error (non-fatal): ${err.message}`);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  // OP4 — join / leave\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  /**\n   * Join a voice channel.\n   * Returns Promise<{ token, endpoint, sessionId }> once both\n   * VOICE_STATE_UPDATE and VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE are received.\n   *\n   * Smart pre-join logic:\n   *   • If already in the TARGET channel and voice state is fully cached,\n   *     skip the disconnect/rejoin and return cached state immediately.\n   *     This prevents a spurious VOICE_STATE_UPDATE(channel_id: null) from\n   *     racing against Lavalink's handshake.\n   *   • If in a DIFFERENT channel, disconnect first (500ms grace) then join.\n   *   • If not in any channel, join directly.\n   */\n  joinVoiceChannel(guildId, channelId) {\n    return new Promise(async (resolve, reject) => {\n      const guild = this.client.guilds.cache.get(guildId);\n      if (!guild) {\n        return reject(new Error(`Guild ${guildId} not in cache`));\n\n[405 more lines in file. Use offset=250 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777310986115}}
{"type":"message","id":"14def9af","parentId":"2b7d27c0","timestamp":"2026-04-27T17:29:46.126Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"ollama_call_5bd766e9-46d4-471a-bef3-026868a2ba49","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"      }\n\n      // Check current voice state via discord.js cache\n      const me = guild.members.cache.get(BOT_USER_ID);\n      const currentChannel = me?.voice?.channelId ?? null;\n\n      // If already in the correct channel AND we have a full cached state, reuse it.\n      const cached = this.voiceStates.get(guildId);\n      if (currentChannel === channelId && cached?.token && cached?.endpoint && cached?.sessionId) {\n        log('VOICE', `Already in channel ${channelId} (guild=${guildId}), reusing cached voice state`);\n        return resolve(cached);\n      }\n\n      // Evict any existing adapter BEFORE we touch OP4 — critical step\n      this._evictVoiceAdapter(guildId);\n\n      // Clear stale voice state so we wait for fresh packets\n      this.voiceStates.delete(guildId);\n\n      // If in a different channel, disconnect first to force fresh events\n      if (currentChannel && currentChannel !== channelId) {\n        log('VOICE', `Moving from channel=${currentChannel} → ${channelId} (guild=${guildId})`);\n        guild.shard.send({ op: 4, d: { guild_id: guildId, channel_id: null, self_mute: false, self_deaf: false } });\n        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 500));\n        // Evict again — disconnect OP4 may have re-triggered adapter creation internally\n        this._evictVoiceAdapter(guildId);\n      }\n\n      // Send OP4 join\n      guild.shard.send({\n        op: 4,\n        d: { guild_id: guildId, channel_id: channelId, self_mute: false, self_deaf: true },\n      });\n      log('VOICE', `OP4 join → guild=${guildId} channel=${channelId}`);\n\n      const timeout = setTimeout(() => {\n        this.pendingVoice.delete(guildId);\n        reject(new Error('Voice join timeout (10s) — no VOICE_STATE_UPDATE + VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE received'));\n      }, 10_000);\n\n      this.pendingVoice.set(guildId, { resolve, reject, timeout });\n    });\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Leave a voice channel (OP4 null-channel).\n   */\n  leaveVoiceChannel(guildId) {\n    const guild = this.client.guilds.cache.get(guildId);\n    if (guild) {\n      this._evictVoiceAdapter(guildId);\n      guild.shard.send({ op: 4, d: { guild_id: guildId, channel_id: null, self_mute: false, self_deaf: false } });\n    }\n    this.voiceStates.delete(guildId);\n    this.activeChannels.delete(guildId);\n    this.activeTracks.delete(guildId);\n    log('VOICE', `Left guild=${guildId}`);\n  }\n\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  // Lavalink WebSocket — session management\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  _connectLavalink() {\n    const url = `ws://${LAVALINK_HOST}:${LAVALINK_PORT}/v4/websocket`;\n    log('LAVALINK', `Connecting to ${url}`);\n\n    this.lavalinkWs = new WebSocket(url, {\n      headers: {\n        Authorization: LAVALINK_PASS,\n        'User-Id': BOT_USER_ID,\n        'Client-Name': 'RanaVoiceBridge/2.0',\n      },\n    });\n\n    this.lavalinkWs.on('open', () => {\n      log('LAVALINK', 'WS connected');\n    });\n\n    this.lavalinkWs.on('message', (data) => {\n      let msg;\n      try { msg = JSON.parse(data); } catch { return; }\n\n      if (msg.op === 'ready') {\n        this.lavalinkSessionId = msg.sessionId;\n        log('LAVALINK', `Session ready: ${msg.sessionId} (resumed=${msg.resumed})`);\n      } else if (msg.op === 'event') {\n        this._handleLavalinkEvent(msg);\n      }\n      // playerUpdate is noisy — skip\n    });\n\n    this.lavalinkWs.on('close', (code) => {\n      log('LAVALINK', `Disconnected (code=${code}). Reconnecting in 5s...`);\n      this.lavalinkSessionId = null;\n      setTimeout(() => this._connectLavalink(), 5_000);\n    });\n\n    this.lavalinkWs.on('error', (err) => {\n      log('LAVALINK', `WS error: ${err.message}`);\n\n[305 more lines in file. Use offset=350 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777310986121}}
{"type":"message","id":"776d21a0","parentId":"14def9af","timestamp":"2026-04-27T17:30:38.454Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"我理解問題了。根據指令，我需要在 voice_bridge.js 中：\n\n1. **完全刪除**所有創建新 Client 的邏輯（`this.client = new Client({...})`）\n2. **移除** `this.client.login()` 的調用\n3. **只保留**接收外部傳入的 `client` 參數\n\n然後需要將 VoiceBridge 的初始化注入到主進程。\n\n讓我讀取 voice_bridge.js 並完全重寫它，移除所有 client 創建和 login 邏輯。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"ollama_call_e12213a5-0358-45d8-8625-f65c323e7603","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\workspace\\services\\music_core\\voice_bridge.js"}}],"stopReason":"toolUse","api":"ollama","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen3.5:9b","usage":{"input":57741,"output":159,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":57900,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"timestamp":1777311038454}}
{"type":"message","id":"54405387","parentId":"776d21a0","timestamp":"2026-04-27T17:30:38.515Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"ollama_call_e12213a5-0358-45d8-8625-f65c323e7603","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * voice_bridge.js — Rana Voice Gateway Bridge v2.0\n * =================================================\n * FIX: Raw Gateway Forwarding — eliminates the competing-Client conflict.\n *\n * ── ROOT CAUSE (v1) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n *   voice_bridge.js spawned its own discord.js Client with the same bot token\n *   as OpenClaw. Both Clients received the same gateway packets. The sequence:\n *\n *     voice_bridge OP4 join\n *       → Discord dispatches VOICE_STATE_UPDATE + VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE to BOTH shards\n *       → OpenClaw's discord.js internal voice.adapters fires cleanup\n *       → cleanup emits OP4 disconnect on OpenClaw's shard\n *       → Lavalink's voice UDP is invalidated → WebSocketClosedEvent (4014 / 4006)\n *       → playback dies immediately after TrackStartEvent\n *\n *   Secondary bugs in v1:\n *     • `channelId` included in the Lavalink v4 `voice` body (invalid field → silent ignore or reject)\n *     • Pre-join disconnect always fired, even when bot was already in the correct channel,\n *       creating a spurious VOICE_STATE_UPDATE(channel_id: null) that raced Lavalink's handshake.\n *     • No WebSocketClosedEvent recovery — once Lavalink dropped the voice conn, it stayed dead.\n *\n * ── v2 FIX STRATEGY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n *   1.  VoiceBridge is an OpenClaw Extension — it ACCEPTS OpenClaw's existing Client\n *       instead of calling client.login() again. One gateway session. Zero competition.\n *   2.  discord.js voice adapters are forcibly evicted for managed guilds BEFORE every\n *       OP4 send. This prevents discord.js from calling adapter.onVoiceStateUpdate()\n *       (which is what triggers the cleanup OP4 disconnect).\n *   3.  Raw VOICE_STATE_UPDATE / VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE are captured via client.on('raw')\n *       and stored internally. discord.js can still update its cache, but since no\n *       adapter is registered, it cannot fire cleanup.\n *   4.  Pre-join disconnect is skipped when the bot is already in the target channel\n *       AND the cached voice state is still valid. Avoids the spurious null-channel event.\n *   5.  WebSocketClosedEvent triggers automatic voice re-handshake: fresh OP4 join +\n *       re-PATCH of the Lavalink player with the new credentials.\n *   6.  Combined PATCH (voice + track) in a single Lavalink v4.2.2 request — voice\n *       object is spec-compliant (token, endpoint, sessionId only — no channelId).\n *\n * ── Integration: OpenClaw Extension (REQUIRED in production) ─────────────────\n *\n *   In your OpenClaw agent entry point / plugin loader:\n *\n *     const { VoiceBridge } = require('./voice_bridge');\n *\n *     // `client` = OpenClaw's existing discord.js Client (already logged in)\n *     const bridge = new VoiceBridge({ client });\n *     bridge.listen();   // HTTP server on :8081, ready for LIVE.py\n *\n *   The bridge will hook into the existing client's raw event stream and send\n *   OP4 through OpenClaw's shard. No second login. No token sharing conflict.\n *\n * ── Standalone mode (dev / smoke-test only) ───────────────────────────────────\n *   node voice_bridge.js\n *   Creates its own Client. Do NOT run alongside OpenClaw with the same token.\n *\n * ── Lavalink: application.yml ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n *   No changes required. Standard v4.2.2 config is compatible.\n */\n\n'use strict';\n\nconst { Client, GatewayIntentBits } = require('discord.js');\nconst http = require('http');\nconst WebSocket = require('ws');\n\n// ── Config ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nconst BOT_TOKEN = process.env.DISCORD_TOKEN || 'MTIwMjk2OTY0MzE2MjAxMzc3Ng.Goj9M2._3mVdx-mokW632KXcyXUP0jqIvy5nxIGDFz19M';\nconst BOT_USER_ID = process.env.DISCORD_BOT_ID || '1202969643162013776';\nconst LAVALINK_HOST = process.env.LAVALINK_HOST || '127.0.0.1';\nconst LAVALINK_PORT = parseInt(process.env.LAVALINK_PORT || '2333');\nconst LAVALINK_PASS = process.env.LAVALINK_PASS || 'youshallnotpass';\nconst BRIDGE_PORT = parseInt(process.env.BRIDGE_PORT || '8081');\n\n// ── Logger ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nfunction log(tag, ...args) {\n  const ts = new Date().toISOString().replace('T', ' ').slice(0, 19);\n  console.log(`[${ts}] [${tag}]`, ...args);\n}\n\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n// VoiceBridge — core class\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nclass VoiceBridge {\n  /**\n   * @param {object}  opts\n   * @param {Client}  [opts.client]   Pass OpenClaw's existing discord.js Client.\n   *                                  If omitted, a standalone Client is created.\n   * @param {boolean} [opts._standalone]  Set internally when running as main script.\n   */\n  constructor(opts = {}) {\n    /** @type {Client} */\n    this.client = opts.client || null;\n    this._ownsClient = !opts.client;          // true = we created and must login\n    this._standalone = opts._standalone || false;\n\n    // Lavalink WS state\n    this.lavalinkWs = null;\n    this.lavalinkSessionId = null;\n\n    // Voice state per guild: { token, endpoint, sessionId }\n    this.voiceStates = new Map();\n    // Pending join promises: { resolve, reject, timeout }\n    this.pendingVoice = new Map();\n    // Last known active channel per guild (for WebSocketClosedEvent recovery)\n    this.activeChannels = new Map();   // guildId → channelId\n    // Last stream URL per guild (for recovery re-PATCH)\n    this.activeTracks = new Map();   // guildId → { streamUrl }\n\n    // HTTP server (lazy-created in listen())\n    this._server = null;\n  }\n\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  // Boot\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  /**\n   * Start the bridge.\n   * If we own the Client, logs in first. Otherwise hooks immediately.\n   * Starts the Lavalink WS and HTTP server.\n   */\n  async listen() {\n    if (this._ownsClient) {\n      this.client = new Client({\n        intents: [\n          GatewayIntentBits.Guilds,\n          GatewayIntentBits.GuildVoiceStates,\n        ],\n      });\n      this._hookGateway();\n\n      await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n        this.client.once('ready', resolve);\n        this.client.once('error', reject);\n        this.client.login(BOT_TOKEN).catch(reject);\n      });\n\n      log('DISCORD', `Logged in as ${this.client.user.tag} (standalone mode)`);\n      log('DISCORD', `Guilds: ${this.client.guilds.cache.map(g => `${g.name}(${g.id})`).join(', ')}`);\n    } else {\n      // Extension mode — client already logged in\n      if (!this.client.isReady()) {\n        await new Promise(r => this.client.once('ready', r));\n      }\n      this._hookGateway();\n      log('DISCORD', `Attached to OpenClaw client (${this.client.user.tag}) — no second login`);\n    }\n\n    this._connectLavalink();\n    this._startHttpServer();\n  }\n\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  // Gateway hook\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  _hookGateway() {\n    this.client.on('raw', (packet) => {\n      //\n      // We intercept VOICE_STATE_UPDATE and VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE here.\n      // discord.js will still update its internal cache, but because we evict\n      // voice adapters before every OP4, there is no registered adapter to\n      // call onVoiceStateUpdate() / onVoiceServerUpdate() on — so discord.js\n      // cannot fire cleanup.\n      //\n      if (packet.t === 'VOICE_STATE_UPDATE') {\n        if (packet.d.user_id !== BOT_USER_ID) return;\n        const gid = packet.d.guild_id;\n        const state = this.voiceStates.get(gid) || {};\n        state.sessionId = packet.d.session_id;\n        this.voiceStates.set(gid, state);\n        log('GW', `VOICE_STATE_UPDATE guild=${gid} discordSession=${packet.d.session_id}`);\n        this._tryResolveVoice(gid);\n      }\n\n      if (packet.t === 'VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE') {\n        const gid = packet.d.guild_id;\n        const state = this.voiceStates.get(gid) || {};\n        state.token = packet.d.token;\n        state.endpoint = packet.d.endpoint;\n        this.voiceStates.set(gid, state);\n        log('GW', `VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE guild=${gid} endpoint=${packet.d.endpoint}`);\n        this._tryResolveVoice(gid);\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  _tryResolveVoice(guildId) {\n    const state = this.voiceStates.get(guildId);\n    const pending = this.pendingVoice.get(guildId);\n    if (state?.token && state?.endpoint && state?.sessionId && pending) {\n      clearTimeout(pending.timeout);\n      this.pendingVoice.delete(guildId);\n      pending.resolve(state);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  // discord.js voice adapter eviction\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  /**\n   * Evict any discord.js / @discordjs/voice adapter registered for this guild.\n   *\n   * discord.js v14 stores adapters in client.voice.adapters (a Map).\n   * When an adapter is present, it receives onVoiceStateUpdate() calls and can\n   * issue OP4 disconnect — which is the exact cleanup loop we are killing.\n   *\n   * Called BEFORE every OP4 send so the adapter cannot react to the incoming\n   * VOICE_STATE_UPDATE that our OP4 will trigger.\n   */\n  _evictVoiceAdapter(guildId) {\n    try {\n      const adapters = this.client.voice?.adapters;\n      if (!adapters) return;\n      const adapter = adapters.get(guildId);\n      if (adapter) {\n        log('VOICE', `Evicting discord.js voice adapter for guild=${guildId}`);\n        try { adapter.destroy(); } catch (_) { }\n        adapters.delete(guildId);\n      }\n    } catch (err) {\n      // Non-fatal — log and continue\n      log('VOICE', `Adapter eviction error (non-fatal): ${err.message}`);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  // OP4 — join / leave\n  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  /**\n   * Join a voice channel.\n   * Returns Promise<{ token, endpoint, sessionId }> once both\n   * VOICE_STATE_UPDATE and VOICE_SERVER_UPDATE are received.\n   *\n   * Smart pre-join logic:\n   *   • If already in the TARGET channel and voice state is fully cached,\n   *     skip the disconnect/rejoin and return cached state immediately.\n   *     This prevents a spurious VOICE_STATE_UPDATE(channel_id: null) from\n   *     racing against Lavalink's handshake.\n   *   • If in a DIFFERENT channel, disconnect first (500ms grace) then join.\n   *   • If not in any channel, join directly.\n   */\n  joinVoiceChannel(guildId, channelId) {\n    return new Promise(async (resolve, reject) => {\n      const guild = this.client.guilds.cache.get(guildId);\n      if (!guild) {\n        return reject(new Error(`Guild ${guildId} not in cache`));\n      }\n\n      // Check current voice state via discord.js cache\n      const me = guild.members.cache.get(BOT_USER_ID);\n      const currentChannel = me?.voice?.channelId ?? null;\n\n      // If already in the correct channel AND we have a full cached state, reuse it.\n      const cached = this.voiceStates.get(guildId);\n      if (currentChannel === channelId && cached?.token && cached?.endpoint && cached?.sessionId) {\n        log('VOICE', `Already in channel ${channelId} (guild=${guildId}), reusing cached voice state`);\n        return resolve(cached);\n      }\n\n      // Evict any existing adapter BEFORE we touch OP4 — critical step\n      this._evictVoiceAdapter(guildId);\n\n      // Clear stale voice state so we wait for fresh packets\n      this.voiceStates.delete(guildId);\n\n      // If in a different channel, disconnect first to force fresh events\n      if (currentChannel && currentChannel !== channelId) {\n        log('VOICE', `Moving from channel=${currentChannel} → ${channelId} (guild=${guildId})`);\n\n⚠️ [... middle content omitted — showing head and tail ...]\n\n          discord: this.client.isReady() ? 'online' : 'offline',\n          lavalink_session: this.lavalinkSessionId || 'none',\n          guilds: this.client.guilds.cache.size,\n        });\n      }\n\n      // POST /voice/play\n      if (req.method === 'POST' && req.url === '/voice/play') {\n        const body = await parseBody(req);\n        const { guild_id, channel_id, stream_url, title } = body;\n\n        if (!guild_id || !channel_id || !stream_url) {\n          return respond(res, 400, { error: 'Missing guild_id, channel_id, or stream_url' });\n        }\n        if (!this.client.isReady()) {\n          return respond(res, 503, { error: 'Discord client not ready' });\n        }\n        if (!this.lavalinkSessionId) {\n          return respond(res, 503, { error: 'Lavalink session not established' });\n        }\n\n        try {\n          log('PLAY', `guild=${guild_id} channel=${channel_id} title=\"${title || '?'}\"`);\n\n          // Step 1: Join voice channel (smart: skips disconnect if already there)\n          const voiceState = await this.joinVoiceChannel(guild_id, channel_id);\n          log('PLAY', `Joined VC — discordSession=${voiceState.sessionId} endpoint=${voiceState.endpoint}`);\n\n          // Record active channel + track for WebSocketClosedEvent recovery\n          this.activeChannels.set(guild_id, channel_id);\n          this.activeTracks.set(guild_id, { streamUrl: stream_url });\n\n          // Step 2: Combined PATCH — voice + track\n          const result = await this.lavalinkPlay(guild_id, channel_id, voiceState, stream_url);\n\n          if (result.status === 200 || result.status === 204) {\n            log('PLAY', `SUCCESS: \"${title}\"`);\n            return respond(res, 200, {\n              status: 'playing',\n              guild_id,\n              title: title || 'Unknown',\n              session: this.lavalinkSessionId,\n            });\n          } else {\n            log('PLAY', `Lavalink error ${result.status}: ${JSON.stringify(result.body)}`);\n            return respond(res, 500, { status: 'error', message: `Lavalink ${result.status}`, detail: result.body });\n          }\n        } catch (err) {\n          log('PLAY', `ERROR: ${err.message}`);\n          return respond(res, 500, { status: 'error', message: err.message });\n        }\n      }\n\n      // POST /voice/leave\n      if (req.method === 'POST' && req.url === '/voice/leave') {\n        const body = await parseBody(req);\n        const { guild_id } = body;\n\n        // Destroy Lavalink player first, then send OP4 disconnect\n        if (guild_id && this.lavalinkSessionId) {\n          this._lavalinkREST('DELETE',\n            `/v4/sessions/${this.lavalinkSessionId}/players/${guild_id}`\n          ).catch(() => { });\n        }\n        this.leaveVoiceChannel(guild_id);\n        return respond(res, 200, { status: 'left', guild_id });\n      }\n\n      respond(res, 404, { error: 'Not found' });\n    });\n\n    this._server.listen(BRIDGE_PORT, '127.0.0.1', () => {\n      log('BRIDGE', `HTTP API listening on http://127.0.0.1:${BRIDGE_PORT}`);\n      log('BRIDGE', `  GET  /health`);\n      log('BRIDGE', `  POST /voice/play   { guild_id, channel_id, stream_url, title }`);\n      log('BRIDGE', `  POST /voice/leave  { guild_id }`);\n    });\n  }\n}\n\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n// Standalone entry point\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nif (require.main === module) {\n  log('BOOT', 'Rana Voice Bridge v2.0 — standalone mode');\n  log('BOOT', `Lavalink: ${LAVALINK_HOST}:${LAVALINK_PORT}  Bridge port: ${BRIDGE_PORT}`);\n  log('BOOT', '⚠  Do NOT run standalone alongside OpenClaw with the same token.');\n  log('BOOT', '   Use as an OpenClaw Extension in production: new VoiceBridge({ client }).listen()');\n\n  const bridge = new VoiceBridge({ _standalone: true });\n  bridge.listen().catch(err => {\n    log('FATAL', err.message);\n    process.exit(1);\n  });\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { VoiceBridge };[... 10684 more characters truncated]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777311038506}}
{"type":"message","id":"e9541cdf","parentId":"54405387","timestamp":"2026-04-27T17:32:38.511Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"voice_bridge.js 是延伸式架構（`opts.client` 傳入）。`listen()` 裡只有 `_ownsClient` 時才會 `new Client`。\n\n這意味著它本就可以接收 OpenClaw 的 client，而不需要 `new Client()`。\n\n問題是：**OpenClaw 主程式哪裡呼叫 `new Client()`？**\n\n從之前的搜尋看，`services/music_core/node_modules/...` 中全是套件代碼，不是主程式。\n\n主程式可能根本不存在，或是用其他方式（例如 Python 套件）管理 discord client。\n\n我需要確認 OpenClaw 的入口點，可能是 Python 的 `Live.py` 或 `LIVE.py`。\n\n讓我讀取 `LIVE.py` 確認它是否管理 discord client 或調用 voice_bridge。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"ollama_call_cf9d5123-61d6-4bdf-93a3-d5fe7d389f06","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\workspace\\services\\music_core\\Live.py","limit":100}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"ollama_call_7d0da289-2cc0-45b3-a817-eca32c0e6aac","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"Get-ChildItem -Path \"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\workspace\" -Include \"*.py\", \"*.js\", \"*.ts\" -Recurse | Select-String -Pattern \"Client|client\\.\" | Select-Object -First 20","env":{"OCLAW_EXEC_DISABLE_AUTO_EXIT":"true"}}}],"stopReason":"toolUse","api":"ollama","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen3.5:9b","usage":{"input":65415,"output":331,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":65746,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"timestamp":1777311158510}}
{"type":"message","id":"23ace677","parentId":"e9541cdf","timestamp":"2026-04-27T17:32:38.745Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"ollama_call_cf9d5123-61d6-4bdf-93a3-d5fe7d389f06","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"\"\"\nLIVE.py — Rana Music Core Service v1.1\n=======================================\nFastAPI persistent background service.\nHandles yt-dlp extraction + Lavalink REST API v4 control.\nZero VRAM usage. CPU + System RAM only.\n\nLavalink.jar location: C:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\.openclaw\\\\Lavalink.jar\nLavalink port:         2333 (standard)\nLIVE.py port:          8080\nPython:                D:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\miniconda3\\\\python.exe (3.11)\n\nArchitecture:\n  Discord (text) → OpenClaw tool call → POST /api/play\n  POST /api/play → yt-dlp extract (thread pool) → Lavalink REST → Discord (voice)\n\nRun: D:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\miniconda3\\\\python.exe -m uvicorn LIVE:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080\n\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\nimport logging\nimport os\nimport re\nimport traceback\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nimport aiohttp\nimport yt_dlp\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, field_validator\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Logging\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nlogging.basicConfig(\n    level=logging.INFO,\n    format=\"[%(asctime)s] [%(levelname)s] %(name)s — %(message)s\",\n    datefmt=\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\",\n)\nlog = logging.getLogger(\"LIVE\")\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Config — Lavalink standard port 2333\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nLAVALINK_HOST  = os.getenv(\"LAVALINK_HOST\", \"http://127.0.0.1:2333\")\nLAVALINK_PASS  = os.getenv(\"LAVALINK_PASS\", \"youshallnotpass\")\nDISCORD_BOT_ID = os.getenv(\"DISCORD_BOT_ID\", \"\")\nVOICE_BRIDGE   = os.getenv(\"VOICE_BRIDGE\", \"http://127.0.0.1:8081\")\nLIVE_VERSION   = \"1.2.0\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# yt-dlp Options — extraction only, no disk I/O\n# Platform support: YouTube, Bilibili, Threads, Instagram, Facebook\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n_COOKIE_FILE = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"cookies.txt\")\n\nYTDLP_OPTS: dict = {\n    \"format\":         \"bestaudio[ext=webm]/bestaudio/best\",\n    \"noplaylist\":     True,\n    \"quiet\":          True,\n    \"no_warnings\":    True,\n    \"extract_flat\":   False,\n    \"socket_timeout\": 20,\n    \"retries\":        3,\n    \"fragment_retries\": 3,\n    \"http_headers\": {\n        \"User-Agent\": (\n            \"Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) \"\n            \"AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) \"\n            \"Chrome/124.0.0.0 Safari/537.36\"\n        ),\n        \"Accept-Language\": \"zh-TW,zh;q=0.9,en;q=0.8\",\n    },\n}\n\n# Inject cookie file if present (needed for Bilibili login-gated content)\nif os.path.isfile(_COOKIE_FILE):\n    YTDLP_OPTS[\"cookiefile\"] = _COOKIE_FILE\n    log.info(\"cookies.txt found — authenticated extraction enabled.\")\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Shared HTTP session\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n_http_session: Optional[aiohttp.ClientSession] = None\n\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    global _http_session\n    _http_session = aiohttp.ClientSession(\n        headers={\n            \"Authorization\": LAVALINK_PASS,\n            \"Content-Type\":  \"application/json\",\n        },\n        timeout=aiohttp.ClientTimeout(total=15),\n    )\n    log.info(\"LIVE.py v%s started | Lavalink → %s | Port 8080\", LIVE_VERSION, LAVALINK_HOST)\n    yield\n\n[381 more lines in file. Use offset=101 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777311158740}}
